# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Block internal working files and duplicate copies from the public site.
#
# These paths were publicly readable and returned 200. robots.txt alone did NOT
# stop them, for two reasons: a Disallow only asks a crawler not to index a
# file (anyone with the URL still gets it), and the existing robots rules used
# capitalised paths while Netlify serves these lowercased, so they never
# matched anything. These rules return a real 404 instead.
#
# Both letter cases are listed because redirect matching is case sensitive.
# Nothing is deleted: the originals stay in the repo and in
# G:\LSL Authority Pages\lsl-authority-pages.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Internal content-planning notes (they expose the editorial process)
/lsl_questions/*        /404.html  404!
/LSL_Questions/*        /404.html  404!
/readme.md              /404.html  404!
/README.md              /404.html  404!

# Staging and duplicate copies of the answer pages. Serving the same article at
# more than one URL splits ranking signals, and these copies additionally carry
# a canonical pointing at the apex domain rather than learn.*
/pushed%20to%20github/* /404.html  404!
/Pushed%20to%20Github/* /404.html  404!
/duplicates/*           /404.html  404!
/Duplicates/*           /404.html  404!
